## SQ-CDW-02r | rubber trees in the c3_b1 jungle box (count was 0): is the box jungle, are there rubber trees
> forceload add 32 -1600 191 -1441
sleep 30
> zq count 32 40 -1600 191 200 -1441 minecraft:jungle_log
waitlog \[zq\] count minecraft:jungle_log: \d+ 600
> zq count 32 40 -1600 191 200 -1441 myrtrees:rubberwood_log
waitlog \[zq\] count myrtrees:rubberwood_log: \d+ 600
> zq count 32 40 -1600 191 200 -1441 myrtrees:rubberwood_leaves
waitlog \[zq\] count myrtrees:rubberwood_leaves: \d+ 600
> forceload remove 32 -1600 191 -1441
expect \[zq\] count myrtrees:rubberwood_log: [1-9]
look jungle_log > a few hundred = the box is jungle; then rubberwood_log 0 is a real FAIL (pack feature creativedelight:wild/rubber_tree not attached: kubejs/data/creativedelight/kubejs/_worldgen/wild_crops.json "rubber" rule, creativeworldgen _biome_rules.js). jungle_log about 0 = locate hit a jungle edge: INCONCLUSIVE, needs a box inside the jungle

## SQ-CBP-11r | felsic_block drop count over 50 rolls (table: uniform 1-2 scrap; its __comment says 2-4)
> setblock 0 200 2 felsic_gear:felsic_block
> zc3 loot 0 200 2 minecraft:netherite_pickaxe 50
waitlog \[c3\] done 20
expect \[c3\] loot .*creativeequipment:felsic_scrap x(6\d|7\d|8\d)\b
> setblock 0 200 2 minecraft:air
look 50 rolls of uniform 1-2 sum to about 75 (2-4 would be about 150). Only records which range the table gives; whether 1-2 or 2-4 is intended is the owner's call

## SQ-IDS-02r | /cwglocate batch with the quoted filter answers
> cwglocate batch "minecraft:village_plains"
sleep 5
> cwglocate status
sleep 2
> cwglocate stop
reject Unknown or incomplete command|Expected whitespace
look batch prints its start (or a result / "already running"), status answers; the async batch is stopped at once

## SQ-MIN-07r | fishing-net kelp table rolled AT the river and the ocean (c3_b1 rolled at the console origin)
> forceload add -400 16
> forceload add -48 -16
sleep 10
repeat 30
> execute positioned -400 64 16 run loot spawn ~ ~ ~ loot creativedelight:gameplay/fishing_net/kelp
end
sleep 1
> zc3 items -400 64 16 4
waitlog \[c3\] done 20
repeat 30
> execute positioned -48 64 -16 run loot spawn ~ ~ ~ loot creativedelight:gameplay/fishing_net/kelp
end
sleep 1
> zc3 items -48 64 -16 4
waitlog \[c3\] done 20
> forceload remove -400 16
> forceload remove -48 -16
reject Couldn't parse loot table|Unknown loot table|biome_tag.*(not registered|Unknown)
look river: some oceanic_delight:salmon_eggs (weight 3 of 28), no shrimp; ocean (minecraft:ocean, in shrimp_ocean): some oceanic_delight:shrimp (4 of 29), no salmon eggs. Neither in 30 rolls each = the biome_tag condition reads false (creativedelight/loot/BiomeTagCondition.java)

